    {
      "fileName": "disruptive-stance.json",
      "id": "OEGhbRgW6wRbccns",
      "name": "Disruptive Stance",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "OEGhbRgW6wRbccns",
        "folder": "2VfT9SPI0JDUPeCl",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Disruptive Stance",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "action"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": 1
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>The slightest distraction can provoke your wrath, and you're prepared to foil enemies' actions. As long as you are in this stance, you can use @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Reactive Strike] when a creature within your reach uses a concentrate action, in addition to manipulate and move actions. Furthermore, you disrupt a triggering concentrate or manipulate action if your Strike hits (not only if it's a critical hit).</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 10
          },
